Unlock the udomain, and build no Contact list, when star() fails.

star() handles a de-registration REGISTER with "Contact: *". When
delete_impurecord() fails it means to reply with the record's remaining
contacts, but builds them through a NULL pointer: contact_header is
declared as a contact_for_header_t ** set to 0, and build_contact()
starts with *contact_header = 0 - SIGSEGV, which takes kamailio down.
The list it would have built is freed straight away and never reaches the
reply either. And when the record cannot be fetched the function returns
with the udomain still locked, so every later request hashing to that
slot blocks for good.

Unlock on the failure path and drop the contact building. Not reachable
with the current ims_usrloc_scscf, whose delete_impurecord() always
returns 0; found by gcc -fanalyzer.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/save.c b/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/save.c
index 009ea96..d16766d 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/save.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_registrar_scscf/save.c
@@ -161,25 +161,12 @@ end:
  */
 static inline int star(udomain_t *_d, str *_a)
 {
-	impurecord_t *r;
-
 	ul.lock_udomain(_d, _a);
 
 	if(ul.delete_impurecord(_d, _a, 0) != 0) {
 		LM_ERR("failed to remove record from usrloc\n");
-
-		/* Delete failed, try to get corresponding
-         * record structure and send back all existing
-         * contacts
-         */
 		rerrno = R_UL_DEL_R;
-
-		if(ul.get_impurecord(_d, _a, &r) == 0) {
-			contact_for_header_t **contact_header = 0;
-			build_contact(r, contact_header, 0);
-			free_contact_buf(*contact_header);
-			ul.unlock_udomain(_d, _a);
-		}
+		ul.unlock_udomain(_d, _a);
 		return -1;
 	}
 	ul.unlock_udomain(_d, _a);
